"""cc-usage — account-global Claude usage at a glance, mirroring the statusline.

Live-first: cc-usage pulls the OAuth token Claude Code stores in the macOS
Keychain ("Claude Code-credentials") and queries the same endpoint the /usage
command hits — GET https://api.anthropic.com/api/oauth/usage — so the numbers
are fresh AT ALL TIMES: Desktop app, idle CLI, or a brand-new terminal. No
statusline render is required.

cc-usage is STRICTLY READ-ONLY: it reads the usage endpoint + Claude Code's own
caches, and NEVER spawns a process or touches your credentials. If the token is
unavailable it shows the last cached render (and the weekly deadline it
remembers); refreshing the token is entirely Claude Code's own job.
If it can't refresh (offline, logged out, non-macOS) it stays on that cached
statusline render that ~/.claude/statusline.py mirrors to
~/.claude/.hud-cache/last-stdin.json, labelled "cached" (a degraded
source: only the 5-hour + weekly headline bars, no pace/scoped).

Each window is one continuous bar (2 cells per 10%): colored fill = used, a
bright tick = pacing marker — 5-hour tracks the clock; weekly steps by day
(day N of 7 → N/7). The marker's value shows as a dim [N] bracket on every
line — 5-hour = clock %, weekly/per-model = day-step. Dim rail = remaining:

  <plan>
  ◐ session  █▊──────────┃───  9% [80] | 1h
  ⧗ weekly   ██████████┃───── 52% [43] | 3d 14h
    pace     proj 108% · caps ~12h early       (hidden by default: SHOW_PACE)
  ✦ <model>  ██████████┃███▊─ 74% [43] binding   per-model weekly cap(s)

Gradient colors and value rounding match ~/.claude/bin/hud_render.py, the
shared renderer the statusline uses.
"""

